msgid "Dev MCP"
msgstr ""

msgid "Experimental"
msgstr ""

msgid "This feature is currently experimental."
msgstr ""

msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When you run a Quarkus application in dev mode, you can expose a Model "
"Context Protocol (MCP) server.\n"
"It presents the methods used by the DevUI *MCP tools* (methods you can call) "
"and the data exposed by *MCP resources*."
msgstr ""

msgid "Connecting an MCP client"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Open the **Dev UI** settings dialog and select the Dev MCP tab.\n"
"There you can enable Dev MCP, get the connection details (Default `http://"
"localhost:8080/q/dev-mcp`) and see what clients are connected."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Any MCP client that supports the https://modelcontextprotocol.io/"
"specification/2025-03-26[Streamable Protocol, version 2025‑03‑26] can "
"connect using that URL.\n"
"After a client connects, it will appears on the tab:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Guide for extension developers"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Extensions can contribute additional tools and resources to the Dev MCP "
"server. The integration is similar to contributing to the xref:dev-ui."
"adoc[Dev UI], but descriptions are mandatory.\n"
"A single JSON‑RPC service can be used for both Dev UI and Dev MCP; methods "
"without a description only show up in Dev UI, while methods with a "
"description appear in both."
msgstr ""

msgid "MCP resources"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A resource is data exposed by your extension. There are two ways to create a "
"resource."
msgstr ""

msgid "MCP Resources against build time data"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Build‑time data that is already exposed to the xref:dev-ui.adoc#optional-"
"build-time-data[Dev UI] can also be made available to Dev MCP. Provide a "
"description when calling `addBuildTimeData()`:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The extra `description` argument is new: without it the data only appears in "
"the Dev UI. Once supplied, the `jokes` data becomes an MCP resource."
msgstr ""

msgid "MCP Resources against a recorded value"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To expose recorded values (data produced at runtime by a recorder) as an MCP "
"resource, define a xref:dev-ui.adoc#jsonrpc-against-a-recorded-"
"value[build‑time action] in the deployment module. The action must include a "
"description:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Return or produce a `BuildTimeActionBuildItem`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use the builder to configure the action."
msgstr ""

msgid "Set a human‑readable description."
msgstr ""

msgid "Provide the runtime value returned by your recorder."
msgstr ""

msgid "MCP tools"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A tool corresponds to a method that a client can call. Any JSON‑RPC method "
"can be exposed as a tool by supplying descriptions on the method and its "
"parameters.\n"
"Tools can run on either the runtime or deployment classpath."
msgstr ""

msgid "MCP Tools against the Runtime classpath"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To expose runtime information or actions (for example, changing log levels), "
"define a xref:dev-ui.adoc#jsonrpc-against-the-runtime-classpath[JSON‑RPC "
"service] in your runtime or runtime‑dev module and annotate the methods and "
"parameters with `@JsonRpcDescription`:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Description of the method."
msgstr ""

msgid "Description of each parameter."
msgstr ""

msgid "You must register the JSON‑RPC service in the deployment module:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Produce a `JsonRPCProvidersBuildItem`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Specify the class in your runtime or runtime‑dev module that contains the "
"methods."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`@JsonRpcDescription` is mandatory for Dev MCP; without it the method is "
"only available in the Dev UI.\n"
"The method can return primitives, `String`, `JsonObject`, `JsonArray`, or "
"any POJO that can be serialised to JSON.\n"
"Asynchronous methods (`Uni`, `CompletionStage` or methods annotated with "
"`@NonBlocking`) are also supported."
msgstr ""

msgid "MCP Tools against the Deployment classpath"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Sometimes you need to run xref:dev-ui.adoc#jsonrpc-against-the-deployment-"
"classpath[actions on the deployment classpath] (for example, writing "
"configuration files). In that case you do not create a JSON‑RPC service; "
"instead you provide a supplier via a `BuildTimeActionBuildItem`:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The code in the `function` runs on the deployment classpath. The function "
"can return a plain value, a `CompletionStage` or `CompletableFuture` for "
"asynchronous work."
msgstr ""

msgid "JSON‑RPC usage"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default all JSON‑RPC methods are visible in the Dev UI. Only methods with "
"descriptions are exposed via Dev MCP.\n"
"You can override this behaviour with the `@JsonRpcUsage` annotation. Pass "
"one or both of the `Usage` enums (`DEV_UI`, `DEV_MCP`) to control where a "
"method is exposed."
msgstr ""
